Now I understand the recipe. For the FileDialogBridge test:
- Sources: unit/experimental_file_dialog_test.cpp + FileDialogBridge.h (Q_OBJECT for AUTOMOC) + FileDialogBridge.cpp.
- The .cpp includes QFileDialog (QtWidgets) — so the target links Qt6::Widgets (and Qt6::Core). Actually QFileDialog is only referenced in getOpenFileNames — linking Widgets is needed for the .cpp TU. But the test only calls the QSettings helpers. The target must still compile FileDialogBridge.cpp which references QFileDialog → link Qt6::Widgets + Qt6::Gui (Widgets pulls Gui transitively).
- Includes: ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/include + src/app/experimental.
- No jtml_coordinator/JTA libs needed (FileDialogBridge is QtCore+Widgets only).
- Link Qt6::Core + Qt6::Widgets + Catch2::Catch2WithMain.
- rpath not needed (no jtml_compute) — but harmless; keep minimal (no rpath lines needed since no build-dir .so deps).
- add_test jtml.experimental_file_dialog, LABELS headless, TIMEOUT 120.
- The test sets XDG_CONFIG_HOME via qputenv BEFORE constructing the bridge (the QSettings member is constructed in the ctor).

The test file content:

```cpp
// Copyright 2023 Gary J. Miller Orthopaedic Biomechanics Lab
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0

// Plan 007 review round (ce-code-review 2026-08-12, AC1): FileDialogBridge
// directory-memory pins. Catch2 headless, QtCore-only — the test redirects
// XDG_CONFIG_HOME to a QTemporaryDir BEFORE constructing the bridge (the
// QSettings member resolves the config path at construction), then pins the
// QSettings round-trip without exec'ing a dialog:
//  - rememberDir -> lastDir round-trip per purpose;
//  - purpose-bucket isolation (images vs models);
//  - MRU order + dedupe + the kMaxMruDirs=5 cap.

#include "FileDialogBridge.h"

#include <QTemporaryDir>

#include <catch2/catch_test_macros.hpp>

namespace {

/*A fresh bridge whose QSettings writes land in a throwaway XDG_CONFIG_HOME.
 * The env must be set before the FileDialogBridge ctor (QSettings resolves
 * the path there).*/
FileDialogBridge MakeBridge(QTemporaryDir& dir) {
    qputenv("XDG_CONFIG_HOME", dir.path().toUtf8());
    // The org/app pair matches the bridge's ctor.
    QSettings::clear();  // hmm — QSettings::clear clears ALL settings in the default scope... that's destructive to the REAL config if env didn't change!
    ...
}
```

Careful: `QSettings::clear()` is a static that clears the user's real settings — dangerous. Don't call it. Just set XDG_CONFIG_HOME + construct. Each TEST_CASE creates its own QTemporaryDir + bridge. The env var persists across TEST_CASEs (set again each time — fine).

One catch: QTemporaryDir must outlive the bridge (the dir is removed on destruction; QSettings writes happen during the test). Order: QTemporaryDir dir; FileDialogBridge bridge = ... — bridge after dir → dir destroyed after bridge? C++ destruction order is reverse of declaration → declare dir FIRST, bridge SECOND → bridge destroyed first, dir second. Good.

Also — the qputenv affects the process env for subsequent tests, but each test re-sets it. And QSettings instances created BEFORE the env change would cache... each test creates a fresh bridge. OK.

Also note: QSettings("JointTrackAutoGPU", "jtml_experimental") with XDG_CONFIG_HOME set → writes to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/JointTrackAutoGPU/jtml_experimental.conf. Since FileDialogBridge ctor constructs settings_ with the org/app pair — matches.

Wait — one concern: the settings_ member is constructed IN the FileDialogBridge ctor — with the env set, QSettings picks up the redirected path. Good.

Tests:

```cpp
TEST_CASE("file_dialog: rememberDir -> lastDir round-trip per purpose", "[experimental][file_dialog]") {
    QTemporaryDir dir;
    FileDialogBridge bridge = MakeBridge(dir);
    CHECK(bridge.lastDir("images").isEmpty());
    bridge.rememberDir("/data/studies/Kneel_1", "images");
    CHECK(bridge.lastDir("images") == "/data/studies/Kneel_1");
    bridge.rememberDir("/data/studies/Kneel_2", "images");
    CHECK(bridge.lastDir("images") == "/data/studies/Kneel_2");
}

TEST_CASE("file_dialog: purpose buckets are isolated", ...) {
    ...
    bridge.rememberDir("/a", "images");
    bridge.rememberDir("/b", "models");
    CHECK(bridge.lastDir("images") == "/a");
    CHECK(bridge.lastDir("models") == "/b");
    CHECK(bridge.lastDir("general").isEmpty());
}

TEST_CASE("file_dialog: MRU order, dedupe, cap", ...) {
    ...
    bridge.rememberDir("/d1", "images");
    bridge.rememberDir("/d2", "images");
    bridge.rememberDir("/d3", "images");
    bridge.rememberDir("/d4", "images");
    bridge.rememberDir("/d5", "images");
    // Cap: 6th entry evicts the oldest.
    bridge.rememberDir("/d6", "images");
    const auto urls = bridge.mruUrls("images");
    REQUIRE(urls.size() == 5);
    CHECK(urls[0].toLocalFile() == "/d6");
    CHECK(urls[4].toLocalFile() == "/d2");
    // Dedupe: re-remembering an existing entry moves it to the front.
    bridge.rememberDir("/d3", "images");
    const auto urls2 = bridge.mruUrls("images");
    REQUIRE(urls2.size() == 5);
    CHECK(urls2[0].toLocalFile() == "/d3");
    CHECK(urls2[1].toLocalFile() == "/d6");
    CHECK(urls2.size() == 5);
    // d1 was evicted
    for (const auto& u : urls2) CHECK(u.toLocalFile() != "/d1");
}
